          "In a world of kings, pharaohs and emperors, one Greek city decided that the decisions would be made by the assembly of its citizens. The word says it: demos (people) plus kratos (power).",
          "It wasn't like voting every four years today. It was direct: some forty times a year, several thousand citizens gathered on the hill of the Pnyx, anyone could ask to speak, and war, taxes, treaties or someone's exile were settled by a show of hands.",
