              "THE USUAL PROCEDURE. We still have the letter in which Pliny, governor of Bithynia, asks the emperor Trajan what to do with them, and the reply: don't go looking for them, but if someone denounces them and they refuse to recant, they must be executed. The test was to burn incense before the emperor's image, and whoever did it went home. That's the point to grasp: those who died, died for refusing to make a gesture.",
