          "It was also an age of inventions that would take centuries to reach Europe: paper, the wheelbarrow, the breast-strap harness for horses, the sternpost rudder, cast iron, the water mill, the magnetic compass and the first seismograph — a bronze contraption that in the year 132 detected an earthquake hundreds of kilometers away.",
          "And to the west they opened the route that would change the world. Emperor Wu sent an explorer, Zhang Qian, to look for allies against the northern nomads, and he came back thirteen years later with news of unknown kingdoms, cities and horses. Out of that came the network of roads we call the Silk Road.",
