          "Before paper, writing was expensive and unwieldy. In China they used strips of bamboo tied together with cord — a single book could weigh tens of kilos and fill a cart — or silk, which was ruinously expensive. In the West they used papyrus, which only grew in Egypt, and parchment, that is, animal skin: a Bible took the hides of an entire flock.",
