          "Taxes crushed the small landowners, who fell one by one under the protection of the great landholders and ended up tied to the land: that, in practice, is where the manorial world of the Middle Ages begins — inside the empire itself.",
          "And on top of that, the outside pressure changed scale. The arrival of the Huns pushed whole peoples up against the Danube frontier; in 378 the Goths destroyed the imperial army at Adrianople and killed the emperor; in 410 Alaric sacked Rome, something that hadn't happened in eight centuries; in 439 the Vandals took North Africa and with it the wheat that fed Rome.",
