              "TAXES AND INEQUALITY. The great landowners had the influence not to pay, and the weight fell on the small farmers and the mid-sized cities, which were ruined. When a farmer no longer cares who's in charge because either way his harvest gets taken, an empire has lost its social base.",
              "EPIDEMICS AND POPULATION. The Antonine Plague and the Plague of Cyprian may have killed millions. Fewer people means fewer soldiers, fewer taxpayers and abandoned fields.",
              "THE ARMY. It became the arbiter of politics: it proclaimed and murdered emperors as it suited. And it filled up with units of allied peoples who fought well but were loyal to their own chief, not to the state. When the state couldn't pay them, those chiefs helped themselves.",
              "THE OUTSIDE PRESSURE. It wasn't a «barbarian invasion» storming the gates: in 376 thousands of Goths asked to come in as refugees fleeing the Huns, were admitted, then mistreated and swindled by Roman officials, and rebelled. From there to Adrianople and everything else.",
