          "Its decline had one key, shameful moment: in 1204, the crusaders on their way to the Holy Land sacked Constantinople, the largest Christian city in the world, for three days. It was Christians who struck the blow it never recovered from. After that it survived another two hundred years, smaller and smaller, until 1453.",
