          "The state was governed by examination. In theory any man could sit a punishing set of tests on the Confucian classics, on politics… and on writing poetry: you had to be able to compose poems to become an official. That broke the monopoly of the aristocratic families and created an elite of merit, with a literary culture of its own.",
          "And that's why it was the great age of Chinese poetry. Li Bai, the wandering, drunken poet whom legend has drowning while trying to embrace the moon's reflection; Du Fu, the poet of war and hunger, who chronicled the empire's collapse like a reporter; Bai Juyi, who tested his poems on an elderly servant and rewrote them if she didn't understand them.",
