          "After the Western Roman Empire disappeared, Europe was left divided into Germanic kingdoms at war with each other. Charlemagne, king of the Franks, conquered and joined a great many of them: present-day France, western Germany, the Netherlands, northern Italy and part of Austria and Catalonia.",
          "On Christmas Day in the year 800, the pope crowned him emperor in Rome. That gesture had a perfectly clear intention: to proclaim that the Roman Empire was back, this time Christian and based in the north. Constantinople considered it a usurpation, and rightly so.",
