          "The military result was a failure: in the end, by 1291, not one Christian territory was left in the Holy Land. The historical result was enormous in another direction: Europe was connected to the eastern Mediterranean. In came sugar, cotton, spices, citrus fruit, paper, Arabic numerals, the medicine of Avicenna, the texts of Aristotle, fortification techniques, accounting and the first letters of credit, so you didn't have to travel with gold on you.",
