          "What appeared was a curious legal novelty: a corporation, a guild, exactly like that of the shoemakers or the weavers, but of masters and students. The Latin word universitas means precisely that: the whole, the community. At Bologna (1088) the guild was formed by the students, who hired the professors; in Paris it was the masters.",
