          "The Renaissance begins as a cultural fashion in the cities of northern Italy: recovering the texts, the art and the forms of ancient Greece and Rome. And it starts there for very concrete reasons: Florence, Venice, Milan and Genoa were commercial republics and lordships flush with money, with bankers who wanted prestige and bought art, and with a Roman past under their feet.",
          "The deep change wasn't aesthetic but a change of perspective. Humanism put the human being at the center of reflection — the body, reason, history, the capacity to improve — without necessarily giving up faith. The question shifted from «what does God want» to «what can a human being do».",
          "In art, mathematical perspective was invented, which lets space be represented as the eye sees it; anatomy was studied by dissecting corpses; oil painting reached a new depth; and artists stopped being anonymous craftsmen and became authors with a name, a contract and fame.",
