          "He set out from Palos on 3 August 1492 with three ships and some ninety men, and made land on 12 October on an island in the Bahamas. He died in 1506 convinced he had reached Asia; the continent was named America after another navigator, Amerigo Vespucci, who did argue that it was new land.",
