          "Spain and Portugal set up territorial empires, with viceroyalties, cities, cathedrals, universities (those of Lima and Mexico date from 1551) and a mixing of populations that gave rise to new societies. Their economic engine was the silver of Potosí and Zacatecas, mined with forced indigenous labor, which funded the European wars and reached as far as China.",
          "Holland and England invented something different: the private trading company with the powers of a state. The Dutch East India Company and the British East India Company had shares traded on an exchange, armies of their own, and could sign treaties and declare wars. It was the birth of the multinational corporation and of modern financial capitalism: the first stock exchange in the world is Amsterdam's.",
