          "The thirteen British colonies of North America were prosperous and fairly autonomous, with assemblies of their own. The conflict began over the taxes London imposed on them to pay for the wars against France: the stamp tax, the tea tax, the customs duties.",
          "The colonists' argument wasn't «we don't want to pay», but a political principle: «no taxation without representation». If they had no members in the British Parliament, that Parliament had no right to tax them. When they threw the cargo of tea into Boston harbor in 1773, London's repressive response united the colonies.",
          "On 4 July 1776 they approved the Declaration of Independence, a text written for the most part by Jefferson that begins by asserting that all men are created equal and that they have unalienable rights: life, liberty and the pursuit of happiness. It was Locke and the Enlightenment turned into a country's founding document.",
          "Then they did something even harder than winning: they designed a state. The Constitution of 1787 created a federal republic with a separation of powers, regular elections, a president instead of a king and a system of checks and balances, and it added a bill of rights.",
