          "But his real mark was administrative. Wherever he arrived, he imposed the Civil Code — which abolished feudal privileges, made citizens equal before the law, guaranteed property and separated state from Church — along with the civil registry, an orderly tax system and a professional administration. That code is still the basis of civil law in much of the world.",
          "Three things defeated him. First, the sea: the British fleet annihilated him at Trafalgar in 1805 and he was never able to invade England. Second, Spain: guerrilla war and popular resistance after 2 May 1808 cost him years, money and three hundred thousand men in what he himself called «my Spanish ulcer». And third, Russia: he went in in 1812 with more than half a million soldiers and came out with a few tens of thousands, destroyed by the distances, hunger, typhus and the winter.",
