          "The first reaction wasn't for independence but quite the opposite: governing juntas were formed «in the name of Ferdinand VII». But on taking local power, the Creole elites — descendants of Spaniards born in America — discovered that they could govern themselves, and that they had spent generations shut out of the high offices, reserved for those born in Spain.",
