          "Then came mass application. In 1882 Edison set up the first power station and the first distribution network with incandescent bulbs, and he also created something new: the industrial laboratory, a place where invention happened systematically and as a team. Tesla and Westinghouse established alternating current, which could actually be carried hundreds of kilometers, and with it the modern electrical grid.",
          "The effects on everyday life were immediate and enormous. Clean, cheap light: the day stopped ending at nightfall, you could read and study at night, cities became safer. Electric motors: each machine with its own, which allowed more flexible factories and small workshops. And at home, the fridge, the washing machine, the iron and the vacuum cleaner, which drastically cut the hours of housework — done almost exclusively by women.",
