          "The spark was the election of Abraham Lincoln in 1860. Lincoln wasn't a radical abolitionist: his platform was to stop slavery spreading into the new western territories, not to eliminate it where it already existed. But the southern states understood perfectly well that without expansion the system was doomed, and eleven of them seceded and formed the Confederacy. In April 1861 they opened fire on Fort Sumter.",
