          "The steam engine was enormous, heavy and needed a boiler, water, coal and time to heat up. It was fine for factories, trains and ships, but not for an individual vehicle.",
          "The internal combustion engine solved that: the explosion happens inside the cylinder itself, with a very concentrated liquid fuel. The result is light, starts fast and can be built small. Otto developed the four-stroke cycle, Benz built the first practical automobile in 1886 and Diesel patented in 1892 a higher-efficiency engine for heavy work.",
          "The first long trip was made by Bertha Benz in 1888: she took her husband's car without telling him, covered 106 km with her two sons, bought fuel at a pharmacy, repaired breakdowns along the way and proved the invention worked. It was, in effect, the first marketing campaign of the car industry.",
          "And it changed the physical world. Cities were redesigned around the car: roads, traffic lights, parking, gas stations, residential districts far from the center. Individual freedom of movement grew as never before.",
