        dato: "Fun fact: at the start of the 20th century three technologies were competing on equal terms: steam, gasoline and ELECTRICITY. In 1900, close to a third of the cars in New York were electric. Gasoline won on range and on the price of oil, and it has taken us a century to come back to the option that was already there.",
