          "Maxwell predicted electromagnetic waves mathematically, Hertz produced them in a laboratory and Marconi had the practical obsession of using them to communicate without wires: in 1901 he managed to send a signal across the Atlantic, something many physicists considered impossible because of the curvature of the Earth.",
          "Its first use was maritime, and it became obvious in 1912: the Titanic's distress messages by radio brought the Carpathia and saved seven hundred people. From then on, carrying a radio was compulsory on ships.",
