          "And the political effect was brutal. Roosevelt spoke to Americans from his office in a conversational tone to explain the crisis; Churchill held up British morale with his speeches; and Hitler and Goebbels turned radio into the central instrument of their propaganda, with cheap state-subsidized receivers and loudspeakers in the streets and the factories. The same technology that informs and consoles serves to indoctrinate an entire country.",
