          "The reason it was them is the interesting part. Everyone else was concentrating on power and on lift; the Wrights understood that the real problem was CONTROL. They built a wind tunnel of their own to measure wing profiles, threw out the published data — which was wrong — practiced hundreds of glider flights to learn how to fly, and designed a three-axis system for turning, climbing and stabilizing, which is still the principle of any aircraft today.",
