          "There were two revolutions that year. In February, the bread queues and the strikes in Petrograd turned into a spontaneous uprising; the army refused to shoot at the crowd and the tsar abdicated within days. Four centuries of dynasty fell without anyone organizing it.",
          "The provisional government that followed made one fatal mistake: staying in the war. And that's where Lenin came in, arriving from exile with a three-word program impossible to beat in that context: «peace, bread and land».",
