          "But Fleming couldn't isolate the substance in useful quantities and the matter stalled for almost ten years. It was rescued at Oxford, by then in the middle of the Second World War, by Howard Florey, Ernst Chain and their team, who managed to purify it and show that it cured fatal infections. Since England was being bombed, mass industrial production was set up in the United States, with giant fermenters, in time for the Normandy landings.",
