          "It began on 1 September 1939 with the German invasion of Poland, secretly agreed with the Soviet Union. But it came from further back: German remilitarization, the annexation of Austria, the dismembering of Czechoslovakia with the consent of France and Great Britain, and the Japanese invasion of China from 1937.",
          "The first phase was a disaster for the Allies: Germany conquered Poland, Denmark, Norway, the Netherlands, Belgium and France within months, with a fast war of movement based on tanks, aircraft and radio. Only Great Britain held out, and it did so by winning the first decisive battle in history fought in the air.",
          "The war became global in 1941, through two decisions: Hitler invaded the Soviet Union in June and Japan attacked Pearl Harbor in December, which brought the United States into the conflict. Those two moves sealed the outcome, because they set Germany and Japan against the two powers with the greatest productive capacity and the greatest human reserves in the world.",
          "The eastern front was the most brutal in military history: the war in Europe was decided there and more than twenty million Soviets died there, soldiers and civilians together. Stalingrad and Kursk marked the change of direction. In the west, the Normandy landings in June 1944 opened the second front.",
