          "Close to six million Jews died, two thirds of the Jewish population of Europe, and whole communities with centuries of history disappeared. Also murdered were some 250,000 Roma, hundreds of thousands of disabled people in the «euthanasia» program, millions of Soviet prisoners of war, Poles, political opponents, Jehovah's Witnesses and homosexuals.",
          "It was done by ordinary people, not monsters: engine drivers who drove the trains, secretaries who typed the lists, companies that supplied the gas and competed for the contracts, neighbors who moved into the empty houses. That's what Hannah Arendt called the «banality of evil».",
